# Frontend localization

Rationale: `docs/adr/frontend-localization.md`.

- No component hardcodes user-facing English text. Every string (JSX text, `aria-label`/`alt`/`title`/`placeholder`, a thrown/caught error message shown to the user, a `Table` column header) goes through `useTranslation(namespace)`'s `t()`, or `<Trans>` for text with embedded markup (a link, bold text).
- One JSON resource file per feature namespace under `frontend/src/locales/en/<namespace>.json` (`common`, `home`, `chat`, `challenge`, `knowledge-base`, `grammar`, `writing`, `preferences`, `admin`, `auth`). A component used from a single feature page keeps its strings in that feature's namespace; a component reachable from more than one feature (grep its import sites to check) goes in `common` instead of duplicating its copy across namespaces.
- A **data catalog** (a list of translated records, not one component's copy) gets its own data-namespace JSON keyed by a stable per-item slug instead of a component name — e.g. `challenge.json` for `frontend/src/data/challenges.ts`'s `title`/`description`/`character.name`/`character.description`/`tasks[].label` — rendered via a `get<Catalog>(t)` function reading a template array that keeps non-translatable fields (ids, `chineseName`, `avatarVariant`) in TS. Follow this same shape for any other catalog. `frontend/src/data/chatCharacters.ts`'s `description` field is translated this way (`getTeacherWang`/`getXiaoMing`/`getChatCharacters` reading `chat.json`'s `chatCharacters` key); its `name`/`chineseName`/`avatarVariant` stay hardcoded on purpose — see the ADR's "Out of scope" section before changing that judgment call.
- Within a namespace file, keys nest under the owning component's name (camelCase) — e.g. `{"homePage": {"loading": "..."}}` — so multiple components can share one namespace file without key collisions.
- Pass the namespace explicitly to `useTranslation()` at every call site (`useTranslation("home")`, or `useTranslation(["home", "common"])` when also reusing a `common` string like `t("common:actions.close")`) — never rely on a default namespace.
- `frontend/src/i18n.ts` inits synchronously from bundled JSON (no loading state); `frontend/src/test/setup.ts` imports it too, so tests assert on the real English strings via `t()` unchanged.
